file tools/fixtures/s/scope_trace.sh recovered -- max_paths 65536 to 262144
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scope_map.sh recovered -- five rows widened by union
file tools/s/scope_trace_witness.rish recovered -- claim line 31 to 40 behaviors
file external-research/20260910-030711_the-row-that-expanded-before-it-matched.md recovered -- the census, the defect, the taxonomy; graded A 93 at Field, room declared mixed
file session-logs/date/20260910/20260910-031953_the-row-that-expanded-before-it-matched.kyri recovered -- the dead lap's own record, landing under its own stamp
file construction/ITINERARY.md DIFFUSER block carries both laps; the stash census and the two open questions
scope one lap: recover a lap that died at its send, verify it on metal, and census the stack it was parked in
status GREEN -- scope_trace witness 40 behaviors 0 faults, standing_equipment_scope_rank GREEN, shell_dialect GREEN, all three re-run at this HEAD; paper A 93 at Field; hot scoped roster pass over the staged tree named in the send
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- whether fleet_round_open.sh may drop a stash it has proved redundant. The measure is cheap and exact: a stash whose added files all exist at HEAD, and whose modified files are shared pins, holds nothing a commit does not. Sixteen of seventeen here qualify.
